id: DRAFT-implot-imgui-headless-atlas
trigger_tool: conan|clang++|cmake
phase: testing,runtime
error_signature: font atlas is not built|Calling.*NewFrame.*font|Error loading shared library libc\+\+\.so.*libace_ndk|relocating /system/lib64/.*symbol not found
severity: 2
category: platform,testing,runtime,conan
match_keywords: imgui,dear imgui,headless,font atlas,GetTexDataAsAlpha8,NewFrame,consumer,test_package,ace_ndk,as-needed,DT_NEEDED,implot
title: Dear ImGui 1.92 headless consumers must prebuild the font atlas and drop unreferenced OHOS system libs
root_cause: imgui 1.92 with a backend that lacks ImGuiBackendFlags_RendererHasTextures builds font glyphs lazily; a consumer test that calls NewFrame without any platform backend leaves the atlas unbuilt, the first glyph access dereferences null baked data and crashes (SIGSEGV right after the IM_ASSERT_USER_ERROR log line). Independently, imgui propagates ace_ndk.z/EGL/GLESv3 as system libs; linking them without --as-needed keeps them in DT_NEEDED even when unreferenced, and libace_ndk.z.so pulls the application-only Ace/NAPI runtime chain whose libc++ inline namespace collides with the hnp toolchain libc++.
affected_scope: any Dear ImGui consumer package (implot, implot3d, ImGuizmo, imgui-node-editor, cimgui, custom UI integration) that runs context/frame tests headlessly on an OHOS device without a platform backend.
verification_cmd: ./consumer  # headless imgui+implot frame on device; see rec_command for the working sequence
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: prebuild-font-atlas-and-as-needed-system-libs
rec_description: In the consumer test, after CreateContext set io.DisplaySize/io.DeltaTime, call io.Fonts->Build() and io.Fonts->GetTexDataAsAlpha8() before NewFrame (legacy atlas path), then draw inside an ImGui::Begin/End window so vertices are actually emitted and assert TotalVtxCount>0. For runtime library hygiene add target_link_options(... "LINKER:--as-needed") so the unreferenced imgui system libs stay out of DT_NEEDED.
rec_command: io.Fonts->Build(); io.Fonts->GetTexDataAsAlpha8(&px,&w,&h); ImGui::NewFrame(); ... target_link_options(exe PRIVATE "LINKER:--as-needed")
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: test-package-template-for-imgui-consumers
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: run-consumer-inside-ohos-backend
fallback_description: Initialize the real OHOS platform backend (imgui_impl_ohos) before NewFrame so textures update through the backend; this requires an application shell with NativeXComponent and is not available to plain conan test_package executables.
fallback_command: ImGui_ImplOhos_Init(...); ImGui_ImplOpenGL3_Init(); ImGui::NewFrame()
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: full-backend-integration
forbid_1_pattern: NewFrame\(\).*without.*Build|skip.*atlas
forbid_1_reason: An unbuilt atlas segfaults on first glyph use; the crash hides the real API assertion results.
forbid_1_consequence: Consumer test crashes with SIGSEGV before printing PASS/FAIL lines, misread as platform incompatibility.
forbid_2_pattern: LD_PRELOAD.*/system/lib64/libc\+\+|force.*libc\+\+\.so
forbid_2_reason: Swapping the libc++ at runtime mixes inline namespaces across system libraries and corrupts the whole process.
forbid_2_consequence: Unpredictable relocation errors in unrelated system libraries.
forbid_3_pattern: dummy.*backend|stub.*ace_ndk
forbid_3_reason: Fake backend symbols only hide the missing runtime boundary.
forbid_3_consequence: Test passes without exercising the real rendering data path.
principles: P003,P010,P012
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to: E464,E471
